# NOW lab configuration - copy to .env.lab, which is gitignored.
#
#     cp .env.lab.example .env.lab
#
# Nothing in here belongs in a commit: every value describes ONE desk.
# An explicit environment variable still wins over this file. See
# docs/lab-setup.md for what each key is for.
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE: the vintage Macs. Their address, FTP account, deploy
# folder and metal facts are facts about a PARTICULAR MACHINE, and there
# is more than one of them - so they live one file per machine under
# .lab/machines/, keyed by the id the host already calls it:
#
#     cp .lab/machines/pb180c.machine.example .lab/machines/pb180c.machine
#
# Flat keys here could only ever describe whichever Mac the file last
# named, and two of them (NOW68K_FTP_HOST, NOW_METAL_MACHINE) were the
# same fact written twice with nothing checking they agreed.

# THIS Mac's address, as the guest must dial it. Not localhost and not
# 10.0.2.2 - the guest is a separate machine on the LAN, and the QEMU
# gateway address never answers on real hardware while looking exactly
# like a hang.
NOW68K_HARNESS_HOST=192.0.2.2

# --- Toolchains --------------------------------------------------------
# The toolchain FILE in each case, not its directory. Both are optional:
# without them scripts/build-guests skips rather than fails, because a
# contributor with no Retro68 install is not failing a gate they cannot
# run. Everything else in this project still works.
NOW68K_TOOLCHAIN=/path/to/Retro68-build-68k/toolchain/m68k-apple-macos/cmake/retro68.toolchain.cmake
NOW_PPC_TOOLCHAIN=/path/to/Retro68-build/toolchain/powerpc-apple-macos/cmake/retrocarbon.toolchain.cmake

# --- The Quadra 800 emulator (scripts/q800-68k) ------------------------
# A 68040 under Mac OS 8.1 is not the PowerBook 180c, and nothing about
# timing or memory pressure carries over - but correctness does, and it is
# far cheaper to find a bug here than at the machine.
NOW_Q800_QEMU=/path/to/qemu-system-m68k
NOW_Q800_ROM=/path/to/Quadra800.rom
NOW_Q800_IMG=/path/to/os81-target.img
NOW_HFSUTILS=/path/to/hfsutils

# --- SheepShaver Mac OS 8.6 Carbon UI oracle --------------------------
# Developer tooling only. Supply SheepShaver and legally obtained Apple
# software yourself; nothing in this repository downloads or ships them.
NOW_SHEEPSHAVER_APP=/path/to/SheepShaver-8.6-Oracle.app
NOW_SHEEPSHAVER_VM=/path/to/Mac OS 8.6.sheepvm
# Optional source checkout. `rig` records its exact revision when set.
# NOW_SHEEPSHAVER_SOURCE=/path/to/macemu
# Optional CodeKitten checkout. `install-apps` records its revision when set.
# NOW_CODEKITTEN_SOURCE=/path/to/codekitten
# Optional overrides; these defaults are paths inside the profile above.
# NOW_SHEEPSHAVER_DISK=/path/to/Mac OS 8.6.hfv
# NOW_SHEEPSHAVER_TRANSFER=/path/to/CarbonLib 1.6 Transfer.hfv
# NOW_SHEEPSHAVER_APPS_DIR=Applications (Mac OS 9)

# --- Metal gates -------------------------------------------------------
# Only read when NOW_METAL is set. The machine half comes from that
# machine's profile - `eval "$(tools/lab-machine env pb180c)"` before a
# suite run on its own, or scripts/deploy-68k --test, which does it for
# you. NOW_METAL_MACHINE is what lets MetalMachineGuard check that
# nothing else on this Mac is already talking to the vintage machine;
# without it, half the guard cannot run and it says so rather than
# passing quietly.
# NOW_METAL=1
# NOW_METAL_REPEATS=3

# --- Signed release assembly (scripts/release-dmg) ---------------------
# The three desk facts a signed development DMG needs. The descriptor
# names the CarbonLib installer and its license material (see
# docs/developer-guide/reference/distribution-standard.md); the profile
# is a MACOS team provisioning profile - without one embedded, an
# identity-signed app's restricted entitlements are killed at spawn by
# AMFI, and the Finder reports only "can't be opened".
NOW_RELEASE_SIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Development: Your Name (XXXXXXXXXX)"
NOW_RELEASE_CARBONLIB_DESCRIPTOR=/path/to/release-inputs/carbonlib-1.6.json
NOW_RELEASE_PROVISION_PROFILE=/path/to/release-inputs/mac-team.provisionprofile
